The most common rootkit is the "R3" one, which includes R3 as the only executable. It is not executable and thus can be used to mask malware. The R3 code is as follows:

```c
#include <windows.h>

// The R3 rootkit
void Win32_R3() {
    // R3 is the only executable
    system("r3");
    // R3 will not be able to execute any code. It is not executable.
}
```

It is not essential to use it if you have already successfully removed and removed all malware.
